{"name":"Massage / foam rolling / recovery gear","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/M%C3%A9lange_du_Beurre_de_karit%C3%A9_et_huiles_essentielles_dans_une_boite_pour_massage_02.jpg/960px-M%C3%A9lange_du_Beurre_de_karit%C3%A9_et_huiles_essentielles_dans_une_boite_pour_massage_02.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%A9lange_du_Beurre_de_karit%C3%A9_et_huiles_essentielles_dans_une_boite_pour_massage_02.jpg","caption":"Mélange du Beurre de karité et huiles essentielles dans une boite pour massage 02","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":9,"casual":{"lead":["Foam rolling means rolling a muscle over a foam cylinder using body weight, a practice called self-myofascial release. People use it with other massage tools to feel less sore and more flexible, so they can train more often and keep posture and movement in good shape.","Body weight presses the muscle against the roller. Researchers have reported short-term increases in joint range of motion, with long-term effects unknown, and post-exercise rolling has been reported to reduce perceived muscle pain. Reviews describe the evidence as favouring use as a warm-up more than as a recovery tool. Appearance outcomes have not been studied."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People roll major muscle groups before training as a warm-up or afterward for soreness, usually for a minute or so per area. Massage guns and balls are used the same way. It is commonly combined with stretching and mobility work."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["The sources reviewed do not describe specific risks. Bruising or pain can occur with heavy pressure, and people with circulation problems or injuries are generally advised to ask a clinician."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/M%C3%A9lange_du_Beurre_de_karit%C3%A